From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: St0neWan9 <pawamaba@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:46:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] openarc: embedder: extension window objects and
 action.openPopup()

Plans B125 and B126.

- OACExtensions.windows (class property) and OACExtensionWindow: the
  shell reports its windows, most recently focused first (identifier,
  profile, focused, popup, frame in AppKit screen coordinates, tabs and
  active tabs). The bridge gives each window a stable Chromium window id,
  sets it as the window id of the window's tabs, and lists the windows
  for chrome.windows.get* (ExtensionTabUtil's embedder window list).
  chrome.tabs.query's embedder tab list follows the windows once there
  are any: a tab is active when its window shows it and in the current
  window when its window is the most recently focused one.
- chrome.action.openPopup() opens the popup on the tab like an
  `_execute_action` shortcut and hands it to the delegate, which is
  renamed -extensions:didOpenPopup:onTab: (it no longer comes only from
  the keyboard). The function resolves when the popup's page loaded and
  fails when it closes first or another popup is open.
